# Interlink product rules

Read **CONCLAVE.md** (Interlink handbook) at the repo root for the full handbook. Keep it accurate when product rules change.

## Levels (only three)

- **Member** — Identity only (photo, name, role, ambitions, looking for). Verification fields are optional.
- **Verified** — Identity + business email + LinkedIn
- **BLACK** — paid ($50/mo or $500/yr) or earned; never granted by peer invite

Short version: Identity → Member. Skip verification → stay Member. Add email + LinkedIn → Verified.

Do not block signup on verification. Resume, website, registration, portfolio are optional extras — they do not make someone Verified.

## BLACK CONNECTION ≠ BLACK

Peer invites award BLACK CONNECTION only. They never promote someone to BLACK.

## Intros (no Premier)

- **Member** ↔ Member only
- **Verified** and **BLACK** meet anyone
- Want to connect beyond Members? Become Verified — there is no Premier plan

## UX

- Standing: typeset steel Member · champagne Verified · **black check** for BLACK · **blue check** for trusted (BLACK CONNECTION). Not metal chips. Check SVGs stay checks.
- Checks appear by the name in chat and on profiles
- Never show “Tier N · Name”
- Signup: Identity required; verification optional (skip = stay Member)
- Discover cards: even height, no “verified via LinkedIn/email” list
- Plans: BLACK · Free (no Premier)
- Signup highlights missing Identity sections when incomplete
- Top nav fixed on every screen
- Table booking photos stay compact in chat (thumbnail, not full-bleed)

## Demo

`brianasome@gmail.com` / `Brian812` is the fixed demo owner login. Demo env flags stay off in production unless intentionally enabled.

## Delivery

Website first in the browser. Native app later after the website makes money. No phone-frame shell for web.
